Part of #36692. Please view this PR in context of changes like https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36694.

`CTransaction` gains a constructor that allows direct declarative construction as an alternative to building through `CMutableTransaction`. `CTxIn`'s constructors gain an optional argument to pass the script witness.

It is a conscious decision that `vin/vout` are passed as generic input ranges and that only *their elements* are copied/moved.
Passing the `std::vector` by value and then moving the *container itself* into place would allow the following:

```cpp
std::vector<CTxIn> inputs = ...;
CTxIn& backdoor = inputs.back();

const CTransaction tx{std::move(inputs), ...};

backdoor = ...; // <- modify `tx`, potentially breaking its invariant
```

Kills mutant https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4675:

```diff
diff --git a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
index 473538e..d484547 100644
--- a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
+++ b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
@@ -32,11 +32,11 @@ bool CheckTransaction(const CTransaction& tx, TxValidationState& state)
     CAmount nValueOut = 0;
     for (const auto& txout : tx.vout)
     {
-        if (txout.nValue < 0)
+        nValueOut += txout.nValue;
+        if (nValueOut < 0)
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-vout-negative");
         if (txout.nValue > MAX_MONEY)
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-vout-toolarge");
-        nValueOut += txout.nValue;
         if (!MoneyRange(nValueOut))
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-txouttotal-toolarge");
     }
```

This mutant could lead to an inflation bug, and the only other check that prevents that is in `GetValueOut`.

Add a test that sends one address too far in the future and one too old and check addrman stores both as 5 days old.

The future-timestamp clamp is the only guard against a peer rewriting existing addrman entries with far-future times, which would make them permanently terrible.

Kills the following mutants:

```diff
diff --git a/src/net_processing.cpp b/src/net_processing.cpp
index e25a4afd3d..236658dd32 100644
--- a/src/net_processing.cpp
+++ b/src/net_processing.cpp
@@ -6014,7 +6014,7 @@ void PeerManagerImpl::ProcessAddrs(std::string_view msg_type, CNode& pfrom, Peer
         if (!MayHaveUsefulAddressDB(addr.nServices) && !HasAllDesirableServiceFlags(addr.nServices))
             continue;
 
-        if (addr.nTime <= NodeSeconds{100000000s} || addr.nTime > current_time + 10min) {
+        if (addr.nTime <= NodeSeconds{100000000s} || false) {
             addr.nTime = std::chrono::time_point_cast<std::chrono::seconds>(current_time - 5 * 24h);
         }
         AddAddressKnown(peer, addr);

```

